\## 9.1 PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION



\### 9.1.1 Rendering Optimization



\*\*Structural Principle:\*\* All implementations must meet the performance thresholds established in Sections 4.2.4 and 8.3.1. These are hard requirements, not recommendations.



\*\*Frame Rate:\*\*



| Requirement | Value | Tolerance | Source |

|-------------|-------|-----------|--------|

| Minimum frame rate | 60 | ±5 | fps | Sec 4.2.4 |

| Frame drops (per 100 frames) | 0 | ±1 | frames | Sec 4.2.4 |

| Rendering time (single frame) | 16.67 | ±2 | ms | Sec 4.2.4 |



\*\*Optimization Rules:\*\*

1. All animations must maintain 60fps ±5fps under normal operating conditions.

2. Any animation that drops below 55fps must be simplified (reduce simultaneous animations, adjust easing curves).

3. Frame drops exceeding 1 per 100 frames require reducing animation complexity.

4. Single-frame rendering time must not exceed 18.67ms.



\*\*Input Latency:\*\*



| Requirement | Value | Tolerance | Source |

|-------------|-------|-----------|--------|

| Input-to-response latency | 50 | ±10 | ms | Sec 8.3.1 |

| Transition start delay | 0 | ±10 | ms | Sec 4.2.4 |



\*\*Optimization Rules:\*\*

1. All user actions must produce visible response within 60ms.

2. Transition start delay must not exceed 10ms.

3. If latency exceeds 60ms, reduce transition complexity or pre-calculate transforms.



\*\*Animation Jitter:\*\*



| Requirement | Value | Tolerance | Source |

|-------------|-------|-----------|--------|

| Maximum jitter | 2 | ±1 | px | Sec 4.2.4 |

| Hysteresis | 5 | ±1 | px | Sec 6.3.2 |



\*\*Optimization Rules:\*\*

1. All animated state changes must apply hysteresis (5px ±1px).

2. Snap to final position when within 10px ±2px of target.

3. If jitter exceeds 3px, adjust easing curve to maintain smoothness.



