\## 9.4 SECURITY & PRIVACY



\### 9.4.1 Data Handling



\*\*Structural Principle:\*\* All user input and system data must be handled securely, using the validation states from Sections 7.1.2 and 7.2.1.



\*\*Input Validation Rules:\*\*



| Validation Type | Requirement | Source |

|-----------------|-------------|--------|

| Client-side validation | All inputs validated before submission | Sec 7.1.2 |

| Server-side validation | All inputs validated on receipt | Sec 7.1.2 |

| Validation state | Success, Error, Pending | Sec 7.2.1 |

| Error messaging | Semantic Error (#E53935) | Sec 2.1.2 |



\*\*Data Handling Rules:\*\*

1. All user inputs must be validated on client and server.

2. All validation states must be displayed to user (Sec 7.2.1).

3. Error messages must use Semantic Error color (#E53935).

4. Success messages must use Semantic Success color (#4CAF50).



\### 9.4.2 State Integrity



\*\*Structural Principle:\*\* The global state machine (Sec 8.1.1) must be protected from unauthorized or malicious manipulation.



\*\*State Protection Rules:\*\*



| Rule | Description | Source |

|------|-------------|--------|

| State validation | All state transitions must be valid (Sec 8.1.2) | Sec 8.1.2 |

| Invalid transition rejection | Invalid transitions must be rejected | Sec 8.1.2 |

| State timeout | Processing state timeout: 5000ms ±100ms | Sec 8.1.1 |



\*\*State Machine Protection:\*\*

1. All state transitions must be validated against the transition matrix (Sec 8.1.2).

2. Invalid transitions must be rejected and logged.

3. Processing state must timeout after 5000ms ±100ms and return to Idle.



\### 9.4.3 Privacy by Design



\*\*Structural Principle:\*\* The system must not leak user data or behavior, referencing the anti-telemetry stance.



\*\*Privacy Rules:\*\*



| Rule | Description | Source |

|------|-------------|--------|

| No telemetry | No usage tracking, analytics | Sec 1.3.3 |

| No external API calls | No REST, GraphQL, WebSocket | Sec 1.3.3 |

| No cloud dependencies | Airgapped deployment capability | Sec 1.3.3 |



\*\*Data Protection Rules:\*\*

1. No telemetry collection permitted (Sec 1.3.3).

2. No external API calls permitted (Sec 1.3.3).

3. Airgapped deployment capability required (Sec 1.3.3).

4. User data must not leave the system boundary.

5. All user inputs must be sanitized.



